    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-18T09:38:34+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T09:38:34+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T00:08:34Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T00:08:34Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A large blocking high pressure system persists over the Tasman Sea. An upper level disturbance responsible for precipitation over central and eastern parts will weaken today as a weakening cold front moves across western parts today and across the southeast on Wednesday. A high pressure ridge is expected to develop over South Australia from Wednesday afternoon with weak troughs clipping the southeast in a broad westerly flow on Thursday and Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW006" description="Riverland" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the late morning and afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures around 17.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:10am to 2:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 4 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Very high chance of showers, most likely in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm in the early morning. Mostly sunny afternoon. Winds northerly 15 to 25 km/h turning west to northwesterly during the morning then becoming light in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 11 with daytime temperatures reaching the low 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-20T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-19T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Light winds becoming west to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the morning then tending west to southwesterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 7 with daytime temperatures reaching around 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-21T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-22T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-20T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-21T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog. Slight chance of a shower. Light winds becoming west to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h during the day then becoming light during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to around 6 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
